<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47092" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sūsa</span></b> , ōrum,
		n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σοῦσα, τά,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the ancient capital
				of Persia</i>, now prob. <i>Soos</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 6, 27,
				31, § 133</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Prop. 2,
			13</span></i> (3, 4), 1; <i><span class="en">Curt. 5, 1, 7</span></i>.—Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sūsĭānē</span></b> ,
				ēs, f., <i>the
				province of Susiana</i> or <i>Susiane</i>, in
			which Susa was situated, now <i>Khuzistan</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 6, 27,
				31, § 133</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sūsĭāni</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., <i>the inhabitants of Susa</i> or <i>of
			Susiana</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 6, 27, 31, § 133</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Curt. 5, 3,
				3</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sūsis</span></b> ,
				ĭdis, <i>adj. f.</i>,
				<i>of</i> or <i>belonging to
			Susa</i>, <i>Susian</i>, <i>Persian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ora, Sid. poët. Ep. 7, 17: aula,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 8, 9</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
